 [`fi_endpoint`(3)](fi_endpoint.3.html),
 [`fi_domain`(3)](fi_domain.3.html),
 [`fi_cq`(3)](fi_cq.3.html)
+
+# LOCAL EXTENSION: fi_sendmsg_ev
+
+`fi_sendmsg_ev(ep, msg_ev, flags)` accepts `struct fi_msg_ev`, containing
+`struct fi_msg msg` followed by `uint16_t ev`. The embedded message and flags
+have the same semantics and lifetime as fi_sendmsg. EV is a host-byte-order,
+per-packet entropy value used by an FI_EP_DGRAM provider for network path
+selection; it does not change the destination address, payload or CQ data.
+The provider copies EV before returning. How EV is mapped to the network
+encapsulation is backend-specific; it is not a literal route index.
+
+Providers supporting this operation advertise `FI_SENDMSG_EV` in fi_info.caps
+and fi_info.tx_attr.caps. It may be requested as a capability in fi_getinfo.
+When absent, callers should use fi_sendmsg. A missing or older message
+operations table returns -FI_ENOSYS from fi_sendmsg_ev. This extension appends
+an operation to fi_ops_msg without changing existing operation offsets.
+It does not define receive-side EV metadata; that requires a separately
+negotiated backend contract. This is a local extension, not an upstream API.
